{"cwd":"/Users/user/Projects/myproject-a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"content":"{\"status\":{\"019c6c5a-59fc-7c62-8ec5-829b07c9c219\":{\"completed\":\"**Critical**\\n\\n1. `/Users/user/Projects/otherrepo-1/specs/extensions/8004-reputation.md:258-309`  \\n   - Issue: The extension defines `interactionHash = keccak256(taskRefBytes || dataHash)` with no mention of a domain separator, schema identifier, or the myproject-a/Light‐Protocol formula. myproject-a’s runtime actually computes the agent’s signed hash as `keccak256(DOMAIN_INTERACTION || sas_schema || task_ref || data_hash)` (see `docs/specification.md:39,335` and `programs/myproject-a/src/signature.rs:227-244`). Without including the domain and schema, any `interactionHash` generated by this extension will never match what myproject-a expects and therefore every Solana attestation will fail validation.  \\n   - Impact: Clients, aggregators, or facilitators following the current extension can never verify a myproject-a agent signature — signature checks always fail and the reputation flow on Solana is broken.  \\n   - Fix: Update the server extension to compute `interactionHash = keccak256(DOMAIN_INTERACTION || sas_schema || taskRefBytes || dataHash)` (with `DOMAIN_INTERACTION = \\\"myproject-a:interaction:v1\\\"` and the SAS schema pubkey for FeedbackV1), and make the client/aggregator checks re-derive the hash the same way before verifying the signature. Document that `sas_schema` must be the published FeedbackV1 schema (per `docs/specification.md:193-205`) or include the schema identifier in `InteractionData` so Solana-safe verifiers can reconstruct the same hash.\\n\\n2. `/Users/user/Projects/otherrepo-1/specs/extensions/8004-reputation.md:258-308`  \\n   - Issue: The extension mandates `dataHash = keccak256(uint32_be(len(requestBodyBytes)) || requestBodyBytes || responseBodyBytes)`, but myproject-a defines `data_hash` as the keccak of the concatenated request and response without any length prefix (`docs/specification.md:250` and `packages/sdk/src/hashes.ts:162-183`). The extra 4-byte length changes every hash, so the `dataHash` sent in `PAYMENT-RESPONSE` will not match what myproject-a stores in its `data_hash` field, and the derived `interactionHash` (even if corrected per issue #1) will still be wrong.  \\n   - Impact: myproject-a validators will reject every signature because the preimage differs; validators expect `data_hash = keccak(request || response)` and will never see the 4-byte length they’re being asked to check. This again makes the reputation proof unusable on Solana.  \\n   - Fix: Remove the length prefix and define `dataHash = keccak256(requestBodyBytes || responseBodyBytes)` (where both bodies are canonicalized as UTF-8 or raw bytes per myproject-a rules). Mention client/aggregator helpers such as `packages/sdk/src/hashes.ts:163-183` so implementations compute identical hashes to on-chain myproject-a.\\n\\nReadiness verdict (Solana/myproject-a lens): Not ready — the current hashing/signature assumptions conflict with myproject-a’s on-chain expectations, so Solana agents and aggregators cannot validate the claimed proofs.\"}},\"timed_out\":false}","is_error":false,"tool_use_id":"call_ZCzxABCkwtcE9RdqacdBZb7a","type":"tool_result"}],"role":"user"},"parentUuid":"019c6c57-e2a9-7373-802e-dfcba907221b:000070","sessionId":"019c6c57-e2a9-7373-802e-dfcba907221b","timestamp":"2026-02-17T16:09:40.876Z","type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"019c6c57-e2a9-7373-802e-dfcba907221b:000072"}
